## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic **`AIProviderSection`** SwiftUI surface at parity with `features/settings/components/AIProviderSection.tsx`, following the established P4 feature-view architecture (the `AISettings` sibling + `ToolCard`/`AlertMessageEditor`/`FSMTimelineChart` precedents).

**Delivered (11 files, ~2,430 LOC, each ≤400-line lint budget):**
- `.Adapter` / `.Validate` — pure cores: provider catalogs, layout predicates, validate-request assembly, result→outcome→banner derivation, validate-button rule, cents⇄dollars cost-cap math.
- `.Projection` — input→resolved phase gate (loading/empty/error/data).
- `.Model` — P1/S8 `AiProviderSource` seam (`commitDraft` = web `onChange`; `async validate` = `useValidateAiProvider`), `@Observable` view-model, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, P1/S10 facade.
- `.swift` / `.Views` / `.Rows` — bordered section + freshness chrome; provider/model grid, Azure surface block (flavor + API version + deployments, Foundry-aware), local & cloud validate flows, secure API-key + cost-cap fields, success/failure banner, all chrome states.
- `.Previews` (11 states), `.strings` (41 keys, web keys verbatim), `.Tests` + `.ModelTests` (48 tests).

**Verification (all green, fresh output in the gate log):**
- Isolated SwiftPM build + **48 XCTest, 0 failures** under Swift 6 strict concurrency against the **real design system**
- iOS-18 `swiftc -typecheck` (the `#if os(iOS)` branches) ✓
- `swiftlint --strict` 0, `swiftformat --lint` 0/10, placeholder gate COUNT=0, `xcodegen` wires all 11 files, i18n coverage 41/41
- An actual compile error the isolated build caught (private default-arg) was fixed.

**Honestly DEFERRED:** the full-app `xcodebuild build test` — blocked by **pre-existing, out-of-scope** issues (unstaged `Shared.xcframework`, `DashboardWidgetSize` redefined 15×, 206 co-located XCTest-in-app files, 0 macOS signing identities); zero `AIProviderSection` errors. Ledger row added; gate log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

